  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms the input grid according to the discovered rule.\n\n    The rule:\n    - Every non\u2011zero color appears as a 2\u00d72 block.\n    - For each such block, compute d = top_left_row - top_left_col.\n    - All cells (r, c) satisfying r - c = d belong to the same diagonal.\n    - If the block's colour is odd (e.g. 1) the diagonal is extended\n      backwards (north\u2011west) from the block's top\u2011left corner until the\n      grid border is reached.\n    - If the block's colour is even (e.g. 2) the diagonal is extended\n      forwards (south\u2011east) from the block's bottom\u2011right corner until the\n      border is reached.\n    - Existing non\u2011zero cells are never overwritten.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid:\n        return grid\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n\n    # locate all 2\u00d72 blocks of the same non\u2011zero colour\n    blocks = []\n    for i in range(rows - 1):\n        for j in range(cols - 1):\n            val = grid[i][j]\n            if val != 0 and val == grid[i][j + 1] == grid[i + 1][j] == grid[i + 1][j + 1]:\n                blocks.append((i, j, val))\n\n    # extend each block along its diagonal\n    for i, j, val in blocks:\n        # diagonal identifier\n        # (i - j) is the same for the whole 2\u00d72 block\n        if val % 2 == 1:          # odd colour \u2192 extend backwards (north\u2011west)\n            offset = -1\n            while i + offset >= 0 and j + offset >= 0:\n                if grid[i + offset][j + offset] == 0:\n                    grid[i + offset][j + offset] = val\n                offset -= 1\n        else:                     # even colour \u2192 extend forwards (south\u2011east)\n            offset = 2             # start after the block's bottom\u2011right cell\n            while i + offset < rows and j + offset < cols:\n                if grid[i + offset][j + offset] == 0:\n                    grid[i + offset][j + offset] = val\n                offset += 1\n\n    return grid",
